# A part written like a Map literal is a Map pattern, not a value: it requires
# only its own keys, so a Map with more keys still matches. Compare the pin
# `({k: 'v'})`, which requires an equal Map.
#= {result: 1, inputs: {xs: [1, {k: 'v', z: 2}]}}
def {xs} = import('inputs')
def [a, {k: 'v'}] = xs
a
